      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A woman with coronary artery disease underwent a new imaging technique: dobutamine-stress electrocardiography (ECG)-gated tetrofosmin-single photon emission computed tomography (SPECT). Dobutamine-stress ECG-gated tetrofosmin-SPECT with automatic left ventricular function analysis software programs detected improvement and a biphasic response of dysfunctional myocardium during dobutamine infusion, which suggested viable but hibernating myocardium. Dobutamine-stress ECG-gated tetrofosmin-SPECT with automatic left ventricular function analysis software programs has the potential to detect viable but dysfunctional myocardium with contractile reserve."},
